  "date": "October 2026",
  "abstract": "Covers the EU Cyber Resilience Act, Regulation (EU) 2024/2847, with one current line, the Official Journal text of 20 November 2024 read with its corrigenda and the delegated and implementing acts adopted under it, and two tracked previews: the Digital Omnibus proposal COM(2025) 837 and the public procurement proposal COM(2026) 590. It turns the engineering-relevant obligations into requirements: scope, exclusions, free and open-source software and stewards, operator roles, important and critical product classes (Annexes III and IV, Implementing Regulation (EU) 2025/2392), the Annex I essential requirements and vulnerability handling, the support period and security updates, Article 14 reporting through the single reporting platform, Annex VII technical documentation, conformity modules, the declaration of conformity and CE marking, and the Article 71 dates. It is not legal advice and tells the user to involve counsel.",
